0,Larrakia people - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Larrakia_people,"November 28, 2025 - The Larrakia people are a group of Aboriginal Australian people in and around Darwin in the Northern Territory. The Larrakia, who refer to themselves as ""Saltwater People"", have a vibrant traditional society based on a close relationship with the sea and trade with neighbouring groups such ...",Laragia,Australian
1,Laragiya language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laragiya_language,"March 15, 2026 - These phenomena suggest that the languages originally had, as Laragia still does, markers at each end of the word."" Larrakia Elder Robert Mills of Batji Tours is able to name plants and animals. Lorraine Williams, a Larrakia woman and Research Associate with the School of Australian Indigenous ...",Laragia,Australian
2,First Nations Radio - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radio_Larrakia,"September 1, 2025 - First Nations Radio, formerly, ... Australian community radio station in Darwin, Northern Territory with a broadcast range that reaches Jabiru. The station was established in 1998 by the Larrakia Aboriginal community of Darwin and is managed and controlled by Larrakia Aboriginal traditional owners. First Nations Radio's aim is to promote Larrakia culture and language to Darwin and the surrounding region, combined with news, music and sport ...",Laragia,Australian
3,Spotify and the ARIA Awards Mark a New Era for Australian Music — Spotify,https://newsroom.spotify.com/2025-11-20/aria-awards-partnership-australian-music/,"November 24, 2025 - Their music has been featured on 31 Spotify editorial playlists and streamed 105 million times globally in the past year. Artist Party headliner The Kid LAROI also took home an ARIA, winning the people’s vote for Song of the Year with his single “GIRLS.” · Spotify leadership joined the celebrations throughout the week, reflecting on the global momentum for Australian artists.",Laragia,Australian
4,Larrikin par excellence : Feature Article : Australian Music Centre,https://www.australianmusiccentre.com.au/article/larrikin-par-excellence,"The sonic explorers we meet and hear here include spooners Liz Dall and Fancy Nancy, lip chirper Pedro Petersen, vocal mimic Xe Rui Fa, bell ringers, spanner player John Drummond, tin doggers, lagerphonists, Col-E-Flower and his Vegie music, the brilliant Michael A. Greene, who can whistle one tune while humming another, the Ntaria (Hermannsburg) Aboriginal Women's Choir, washboardist Deborah Lee Smith, whip-cracker Ashley Brophy, erhu virtuoso Shen Pangeng, and relatively well-known Graingerites, all under such headings as Backyard Hackers, Larrikins and Noise. They all have a contribution to make to the Great Australian Symphony.",Laragia,Australian
5,Does Classical Music Need More Aussie Larrikins? | Music Australia,https://web.archive.org/web/20190208231948/https://musicaustralia.org.au/2017/01/does-classical-music-need-more-aussie-larrikins/,"The desire to please has supplanted the urge to provoke. The reason might partly be, as James Koehne suggests in the book Bad Music: The Music We Love To Hate, that Australia’s musical institutions find the cheeky impudence of the Aussie larrikin persona antithetical to their high culture aspirations.",Laragia,Australian
6,The Kid LAROI is now the youngest Australian solo artist to top the ARIA Album Chart,https://mixdownmag.com.au/news/the-kid-laroi-is-now-the-youngest-australian-solo-artist-to-top-the-aria-album-chart/,"February 7, 2021 - Breakout Sydney hip-hop sensation The Kid LAROI has made Australian chart history with his latest release Fuck Love (Savage), becoming the youngest ever Australian solo artist to top the charts.",Laragia,Australian
7,South Florida Classical Review » » CD Review Lara goes Australian,https://southfloridaclassicalreview.com/2008/07/cd-review-lara-goes-australian/,"John serves up the premiere of a fascinating new concerto in an envelope-pushing program that marks the Canadian fiddler’s finest recording since her debut Bach disc. Though cast in the traditional three movements, Matthew Hindson’s Violin Concerto is anything but conventional, with youthful, brilliant, often idiosyncratic music that reflects the rugged spirit of the composer’s native Australia.",Laragia,Australian
8,Laragia | Ethnologue,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/lrg,"A language profile for Laragia. Get a detailed look at the language, from population to dialects and usage.",Laragia,Australian
9,Larrikan music stories at Techdirt.,https://www.techdirt.com/company/larrikan-music/,"At best, the case should have been dumped for the delay in bringing it. Even more ridiculous, the holder of the copyright, Larrikan Music, didn’t even notice the supposed infringement itself, until an exec heard about it on a TV trivia show. Still, bizarrely, the Australian courts repeatedly ruled in favor of Larrikan.",Laragia,Australian
